# A1 passes from "free elective will" to "the form of a pure will". Kant's Willkür (elective will) and Wille (pure will) can be told apart. But S1 itself makes this step: the elective will rests on a pure practical law, so the categories rest on the form of a pure will. Each claim keeps one sense of "will", so I do not count A1 as a bridge.
# "free" in S3 ("free from sensible conditions") means unconditioned by sensibility. That fits "freedom" elsewhere, and it appears only in claims that keep one sense.
